# Never Push Before a Successful Build

Before any `git push` (or creating a PR that will trigger deploy):

1. Run `yarn build` and wait for it to finish with exit code 0.
2. If the build fails, fix the errors and re-run `yarn build` until it passes.
3. Only then commit (if needed) and push.

Do not push “to see if Vercel builds” — local `yarn build` must pass first.

```bash
# ✅ Required order
yarn build   # must succeed
git push

# ❌ Never
git push     # without a successful local build
```
